Build only qemu-rdp and the crates it uses

The workspace also builds qemu-rdw, qemu-vnc, qemu-vte and xtask, and patches crates.io with two git
repositories for them (rust-vnc, rdw). qemu-rdp needs none of them: with the workspace cut down to
keycodemap, qemu-display and qemu-rdp, `cargo vendor` takes every crate from crates.io. build.sh
lets cargo drop the unused packages from Cargo.lock and checks that it changed nothing else.

For wsh-pve (packages/wsh-qemu-rdp), against qemu-display at the commit upstream.env pins.
---
diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index da783bb..698be63 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -2,13 +2,8 @@
 members = [
     "keycodemap",
     "qemu-display",
-    "qemu-rdw",
-    "qemu-vnc",
-    "qemu-vte",
     "qemu-rdp",
-    "xtask",
 ]
-default-members = ["qemu-rdw"]
 resolver = "2"
 
 [workspace.package]
@@ -23,7 +18,3 @@ zbus = { version = "5.0", features = ["p2p", "serde_bytes"] }
 pixman-sys = "0.1"
 qemu-display = { path = "qemu-display", version = "0.2" }
 keycodemap = { path = "keycodemap", version = "0.1" }
-
-[patch.crates-io]
-vnc = { git = "https://github.com/elmarco/rust-vnc", branch = "server" }
-rdw4 = { git = "https://gitlab.gnome.org/malureau/rdw.git" }
